From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ash: NickelOS installer lets the user pick the disk

The installer chose the destination disk by itself. NickelOS's
os_install_service can list the disks it would install to
(GetInstallDestinations, a JSON array, best first) and install to a given
one (StartOsInstallTo). OsInstallClient gets both calls, and the install
screen a "Choose where to install" step after the intro: one radio button
per disk (model, size, device path, marked recommended or removable), the
recommended disk preselected. The confirmation dialog names the chosen
disk, and confirming installs to it. No disks leads to the existing
no-destination step; an installer that cannot list disks falls back to
confirming its own choice, as before.

